WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.133
This is how Sjekka works.

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:05.860
From a crumpled receipt, to the cheapest way to fill your basket.

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:07.560
It starts with a photo.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:08.960
The browser checks it first.

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:13.810
The server turns it the right way up, and puts it in a queue, so you get an answer straight away.

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:17.288
A background worker sends the photo to Google's Gemini.

00:00:17.288 --> 00:00:18.300
Gemini has one job:

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.483
to read the receipt into a strict format.

00:00:20.483 --> 00:00:22.400
The store, the date, and every line.

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:24.053
Then code takes over.

00:00:24.053 --> 00:00:30.459
The answer is validated, unit prices are calculated instead of trusted to the model, and a receipt seen before is skipped.

00:00:30.459 --> 00:00:32.350
The photo is deleted once it's read.

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:33.632
Next, names.

00:00:33.632 --> 00:00:38.266
The same pizza might come back as Grandiosa, Pizza Grandiosa, or just Pizza.

00:00:38.266 --> 00:00:42.473
Sjekka files them as one product, Pizza, with Grandiosa as the brand.

00:00:42.473 --> 00:00:46.010
So you can ask for the cheapest pizza, across every brand.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:48.296
Sizes are made comparable too:

00:00:48.296 --> 00:00:50.784
per hundred grams, per litre, or per piece.

00:00:50.784 --> 00:00:54.430
A six-pack of eggs is compared with a twelve-pack, egg for egg.

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:57.289
Your shopping list is priced in every chain.

00:00:57.289 --> 00:01:03.060
For each product, Sjekka takes the cheapest choice that chain sells right now, at the size people usually buy.

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:05.242
Receipts never cover everything.

00:01:05.242 --> 00:01:11.361
When a chain has no price for something, it's estimated from how expensive that chain is on the products we can compare.

00:01:11.361 --> 00:01:12.840
And every estimate is marked.

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:16.610
Every six hours, Sjekka also reads the chains' new flyers.

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:20.607
Each offer is held up against what receipts say it cost before the sale.

00:01:20.607 --> 00:01:21.717
Some are real deals.

00:01:21.717 --> 00:01:24.160
Others are the usual price, with a red sign.

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:26.954
You can also share a whole year at once.

00:01:26.954 --> 00:01:33.070
A loyalty card history is read straight from the file, with exact prices, and Gemini only names the products.

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:34.479
No accounts.

00:01:34.479 --> 00:01:35.266
No cookies.

00:01:35.266 --> 00:01:37.341
No photos kept on our server.

00:01:37.341 --> 00:01:38.200
Just prices.

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:39.813
That's Sjekka.

00:01:39.813 --> 00:01:41.900
Real prices, from real receipts.
